## 3. Redux Store as Business Logic Container

**Context:** When reviewing Redux slices. Redux should manage state, not contain business rules.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Business logic in reducer
// src/app/store/vagaSlice.ts
const vagaSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'vaga',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    aprovarCandidato: (state, action: PayloadAction<string>) => {
      const candidato = state.candidatos.find(c => c.id === action.payload);
      
      // Business rule in reducer!
      if (candidato && candidato.status === 'EM_ANALISE') {
        candidato.status = 'APROVADO';
        candidato.dataAprovacao = new Date().toISOString();
        
        // Side effect calculation
        candidato.pontuacao += 10;
      }
    },
    
    calcularRanking: (state) => {
      // Complex business calculation in Redux!
      state.candidatos.sort((a, b) => {
        const scoreA = a.experiencia * 2 + a.formacao;
        const scoreB = b.experiencia * 2 + b.formacao;
        return scoreB - scoreA;
      });
    }
  }
});

// ❌ BAD: Thunk with business rules
// src/app/store/feedbackThunks.ts
export const enviarFeedback = createAsyncThunk(
  'feedback/enviar',
  async (dados: FeedbackDTO, { rejectWithValue }) => {
    // Validation logic (should be in domain)
    if (dados.nivel <= 2 && !dados.comentario) {
      return rejectWithValue('Comentario obrigatorio para niveis baixos');
    }
    
    // Business calculation (should be in domain)
    const pontuacao = dados.nivel * 10;
    
    const response = await feedbackApi.criar({ ...dados, pontuacao });
    return response;
  }
);
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Redux delegates to UseCases
// src/app/store/vagaSlice.ts
const vagaSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'vaga',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    // Only state updates, no business logic
    setCandidatos: (state, action: PayloadAction<Candidato[]>) => {
      state.candidatos = action.payload;
    },
    
    atualizarStatusCandidato: (state, action: PayloadAction<{ 
      id: string; 
      status: StatusCandidato;
      dataAprovacao?: string;
    }>) => {
      const { id, status, dataAprovacao } = action.payload;
      const candidato = state.candidatos.find(c => c.id === id);
      if (candidato) {
        candidato.status = status;
        if (dataAprovacao) candidato.dataAprovacao = dataAprovacao;
      }
    }
  }
});

// ✅ GOOD: Thunk is thin, delegates to UseCase
// src/app/store/feedbackThunks.ts
export const enviarFeedback = createAsyncThunk(
  'feedback/enviar',
  async (dados: FeedbackDTO, { rejectWithValue }) => {
    const container = getContainer();
    const useCase = container.resolve(EnviarFeedbackUseCase);
    
    // Delegate all logic to domain
    const resultado = await useCase.execute(dados);
    
    if (!resultado.sucesso) {
      return rejectWithValue(resultado.erro);
    }
    
    return resultado.dados;
  }
);

// ✅ GOOD: Domain contains the logic
// src/domain/usecases/feedback/EnviarFeedbackUseCase.ts
@injectable()
export class EnviarFeedbackUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('FeedbackRepository') private repo: FeedbackRepository,
    @inject('CalculadoraPontuacao') private calc: CalculadoraPontuacao
  ) {}
  
  async execute(dados: FeedbackDTO): Promise<Resultado<Feedback>> {
    // Validation in domain
    const validacao = this.validar(dados);
    if (!validacao.valido) {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: validacao.erro };
    }
    
    // Business calculation in domain
    const pontuacao = this.calc.calcular(dados.nivel);
    
    const feedback = new Feedback({
      ...dados,
      pontuacao
    });
    
    const salvo = await this.repo.salvar(feedback);
    return { sucesso: true, dados: salvo };
  }
  
  private validar(dados: FeedbackDTO): Validacao {
    if (dados.nivel <= 2 && !dados.comentario?.trim()) {
      return { valido: false, erro: 'Comentario obrigatorio para niveis baixos' };
    }
    return { valido: true };
  }
}
```

**Redux Responsibilities (Correct):**

| Redux Does | Redux Does NOT |
|------------|----------------|
| Store state | Business validation |
| Update state on actions | Calculations |
| Call UseCases | Orchestration logic |
| Handle loading/error UI states | Business decisions |

**Impact:**

- State coupled to business rules - can't change one without the other
- Growing complexity - reducers become harder to understand
- Testing difficulty - need Redux store to test business logic
- Reuse impossibility - business logic trapped in Redux

**Detection:**

- `if/else` logic in reducers beyond simple null checks
- Calculations in reducers
- Validation logic in thunks
- Multiple API calls in one thunk
- `createAsyncThunk` with complex logic

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 5.2: "Store como Orquestrador - Redux nao e camada de dominio. Slices devem delegar para UseCases e atualizar estado apenas."

